vulkan: fall back to vkGetDeviceQueue when vkGetDeviceQueue2 returns null

ggml's Vulkan backend fetches every queue through vkGetDeviceQueue2 (since the
per-instance queue handle refactor, llama.cpp #23570). Some older drivers return
VK_NULL_HANDLE from it even for queues they created: AMD 20.x on Windows
(Vulkan 1.2.133, driver 0x800089, Radeon iGPU on a Ryzen 4500U) is one. The
first vkQueueSubmit then fails with "Invalid queue" and the process aborts,
which is how vibe users on those machines lost transcription when sona moved
from whisper.cpp's ggml 0.16 to ggml 0.22.

The queue was created without flags on that path, so vkGetDeviceQueue names
the same queue. Not upstream as of ggml v0.22.0 / master 2026-08-30.

diff --git a/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp b/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
index c1d86aa..5c91aca 100644
--- a/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
@@ -3304,6 +3304,12 @@ static std::unique_ptr<vk_queue> ggml_vk_create_queue(vk_device& device, uint32_
     }
 
     h->queue = device->device.getQueue2(queue_info2);
+    if (!h->queue) {
+        // Some older drivers (e.g. AMD 20.x on Windows, Vulkan 1.2.133) return a null
+        // handle from vkGetDeviceQueue2 even for queues they created; the queue was
+        // requested without flags, so vkGetDeviceQueue names the same one.
+        h->queue = device->device.getQueue(queue_family_index, queue_index);
+    }
     h->device = device;
     q->handle = h;
 
